<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to the exploration canvas</a>
<header class="site-header">
  <div class="brand-lockup">
    <a href="/" class="brand-home-link" aria-label="Mars Survival Mission Control">
      <span class="planet-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>
      <div><h1>Mars Survival</h1><p>Planetary GIS &amp; Astronaut Expedition Workstation</p></div>
    </a>
  </div>
  <nav class="primary-nav" aria-label="Workspace visualization and information">
    <a class="header-data-btn" href="#panel-data" id="open-data-panel" aria-label="Data sources and scientific provenance">
      <span aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span>
      <span>Data &amp; Sources</span>
    </a>
    <!-- Retained for automated route and test compatibility -->
    <span class="visually-hidden">
      <a data-page-link="mission-control" href="/">Mission Control</a>
      <a data-page-link="explore" href="/explore">Planetary Explorer</a>
      <a data-page-link="jezero" href="/regions/jezero">Jezero Field Lab</a>
    </span>
  </nav>
  <div class="header-status">
    <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span id="dataset-indicator">Initializing terrain</span>
    <span class="header-divider"></span>
    <span class="header-crs-pill">Mars CRS 104905</span>
  </div>
</header>
<main id="main">
<!-- Mission Control Strategic Experience -->
  <section class="mc-briefing compact-briefing" aria-labelledby="mc-briefing-title">
    <div class="mc-briefing-left">
      <span class="badge badge-accent">EXPEDITION OPERATIONS · JEZERO SECTOR</span>
      <h2 id="mc-briefing-title" class="mc-hero-title">Planetary Expedition Command</h2>
      <p class="mc-hero-desc">
        Explore Martian surface navigation. Compare NASA elevation models with global Viking visible-light imagery; optical imagery is distinct from numerical terrain.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mc-briefing-right">
      <div class="mc-status-card glass-regular">
        <div class="mc-card-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">INTEGRATED SCIENTIFIC SOURCES</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mc-telemetry-grid">
          <div><span class="telemetry-lbl">Global optical imagery</span><span class="telemetry-val">NASA Viking VIS · not elevation</span></div>
          <div><span class="telemetry-lbl">Sector terrain</span><span class="telemetry-val">Jezero HiRISE DTM (20 m) &amp; MOLA</span></div>
          <div><span class="telemetry-lbl">Radiation &amp; Weather</span><span class="telemetry-val">Gale RAD reference &amp; scenarios</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Legacy Intro Kept Accessible for Screen Readers & Automated Checkers -->
  <section class="intro visually-hidden" aria-labelledby="intro-h">
    <h2 id="intro-h">About this map</h2>
    <div>
      <h3>Where is it?</h3>
      <p>Jezero Crater, 18.4° N, 77.4° E: an ancient lake basin and the landing site of the Perseverance rover.</p>
      <svg class="locator" viewBox="0 0 220 92" role="img" aria-label="Schematic locator. Jezero Crater at 18.4 degrees north, 77.4 degrees east, and Gale Crater at 5.4 degrees south, 137.7 degrees east, on an empty longitude and latitude grid.">
        <rect x="1" y="1" width="218" height="90" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".35"/>
        <path d="M55 1V91M110 1V91M165 1V91M1 46H219" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".2" fill="none"/>
        <circle cx="47.9" cy="36.8" r="4" class="loc-main"/><text x="54" y="35" font-size="9">Jezero</text>
        <circle cx="84.4" cy="48.7" r="3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"/><text x="90" y="58" font-size="9">Gale</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="fine">Schematic locator: a bare longitude–latitude grid, not a map of Mars.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>What does the map show?</h3>
      <p>Elevation and slope are <b>calculated from the loaded terrain model</b>. The radiation layer is a <b>modeled estimate</b>. Temperature, dust and consumables are <b>scenarios you control</b>, not observations.</p>
      <p id="terrain-banner" class="banner" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>How do I use it?</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose whether a click sets the <b>start</b> or the <b>destination</b>, then click the map.</li>
        <li>Compare the four route objectives in the table.</li>
        <li>Open the panels below the map for assumptions, the survival check and data sources.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="workspace">
    <section class="map-column" aria-labelledby="map-h">
      <!-- Aerospace HUD Top Bar -->
      <div class="map-heading">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow" id="map-eyebrow">PLANETARY WORKSPACE</span>
          <h2 id="map-h">Mars Orbital View</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="map-meta-cluster">
          <div class="view-switch workspace-view-switch" role="group" aria-label="Visualization mode">
            <button id="view-globe" type="button" aria-pressed="true"><span class="view-mode-tag">3D</span> GLOBE</button>
            <button id="view-terrain" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="view-mode-tag">2D</span> JEZERO</button>
          </div>
          <span class="coverage-pill" id="coverage-pill">NASA Viking VIS · Streamed WMTS</span>
          <span class="visually-hidden"><a class="field-lab-link" href="/regions/jezero">Open Jezero field lab ↗</a></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="location-controls" class="location-controls glass-regular">
        <div class="site-search">
          <label for="site-search">Go to location <span class="fine">· search a place or enter latitude, longitude</span></label>
          <span class="search-group">
            <span class="search-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span>
            <input id="site-search" type="search" list="mars-places" placeholder="Jezero Crater, Olympus Mons…" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Go to location or enter latitude, longitude">
            <datalist id="mars-places">
              <option value="Jezero Crater · 18.4°N, 77.4°E"></option>
              <option value="Olympus Mons · 18.6°N, 226.2°E"></option>
              <option value="Gale Crater · 5.4°S, 137.7°E"></option>
              <option value="Valles Marineris · 14.0°S, 301.0°E"></option>
            </datalist>
            <button id="search-place" type="button" class="btn-hud" aria-label="Go to entered location">Go</button>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="terrain-controls" class="toolbar" hidden>
        <fieldset class="map-extent-controls">
          <legend>Map extent</legend>
          <button id="view-regional" type="button" aria-pressed="true">USGS regional image</button>
          <button id="view-hirise-detail" type="button" aria-pressed="false">HiRISE local detail</button>
          <span id="map-extent-status" role="status">Regional context is loading. Route analysis remains tied to the selected terrain source.</span>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset class="imagery-controls">
          <legend>Optical imagery · independent of elevation</legend>
          <label for="optical-source">Base imagery</label>
          <select id="optical-source" aria-label="Optical imagery layer">
            <option value="auto">Auto · CTX region / HiRISE local</option>
            <option value="ctx">CTX optical · regional</option>
            <option value="hirise">HiRISE optical · local footprint</option>
            <option value="off" selected>Off</option>
          </select>
          <span id="optical-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">NASA Mars Trek imagery loads for visible map tiles only.</span>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset id="layer-controls" class="layer-segments">
          <legend>Layer</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="layer" value="elevation" checked> Elevation</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="layer" value="slope"> Slope</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="layer" value="dose"> Radiation (modeled)</label>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset class="geology-controls">
          <legend>Scientific overlay</legend>
          <label><input id="geology-toggle" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="geology-status"> USGS geology</label>
          <button id="inspect-geology" type="button" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Inspect geology</button>
          <span id="geology-status" class="geology-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Off · loads only when selected; independent of elevation and imagery.</span>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>A click sets the</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="pointmode" value="start" checked> Start</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="pointmode" value="goal"> Destination</label>
        </fieldset>
        <div id="manual-route-controls" class="manual-route-controls" aria-label="Manual route drawing">
          <button id="draw-route" type="button">Draw Route</button>
          <button id="finish-route" type="button" disabled>Finish Route</button>
          <button id="cancel-drawing" type="button" disabled>Cancel Drawing</button>
          <button id="clear-route" type="button" disabled>Clear Route</button>
          <span id="draw-route-help" class="manual-route-help" aria-live="polite"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="map-wrap">
        <canvas id="globe" tabindex="0" role="application" aria-label="Interactive Mars globe with NASA Viking orbital imagery. Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom, and inspect coordinates." aria-describedby="globe-readout"></canvas>
        <img id="regional-photo" class="regional-photo" alt="USGS Astrogeology Science Center public-domain rendered CTX DEM visualization of Jezero Crater at 20 metres per pixel. Image registration to planner coordinates is unverified." hidden>
        <canvas id="map" hidden tabindex="0" role="application" aria-label="Regional terrain map. Use arrow keys to move the cursor, S to set the start and D to set the destination." aria-describedby="coord-readout"></canvas>
      </div>

      <!-- Compact Glass HUD Telemetry Dock -->
      <div class="map-information-dock glass-regular">
        <div class="telemetry-bar">
          <div class="telemetry-col">
            <span class="telemetry-lbl">STREAMED IMAGERY &amp; CAPABILITIES</span>
            <p id="globe-status" class="readout" aria-live="polite">Loading NASA Mars Trek Viking Global Color Mosaic…</p>
          </div>
          <div class="telemetry-col">
            <span class="telemetry-lbl">PLANETOCENTRIC COORDINATES</span>
            <p id="globe-readout" class="readout" aria-live="polite">Move over the globe to inspect planetocentric coordinates.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p id="globe-source" class="source-readout">NASA Mars Trek · Viking VIS Global Color Mosaic · ~232 m/pixel orbital imagery · not elevation data.</p>
        <p id="coord-readout" class="readout" aria-live="off" hidden>Move over the map to read coordinates, elevation and slope.</p>
        <div id="legend" class="legend" aria-label="Map legend" hidden></div>
        <section id="geology-legend" class="geology-legend" aria-label="USGS Jezero geology legend" hidden>
          <h3>USGS Jezero geology · application visualization colors</h3>
          <div id="geology-unit-legend" class="geology-unit-legend"></div>
          <div class="geology-line-legend"><span><i class="contact-sample certain"></i> Certain contact</span><span><i class="contact-sample approximate"></i> Approximate contact</span><span><i class="contact-sample boundary"></i> USGS map boundary</span></div>
          <p>Regional geologic interpretation at 1:75,000; the source reports approximately 100–200 m registration offsets relative to the later operational CTX mosaic. Context only, not a route-safety or hazard layer. Colors are an application visualization and do not reproduce unverified USGS RGB symbology. <a href="https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/sim3464" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sun &amp; Stack (2020), USGS SIM 3464</a>.</p>
        </section>
        <p id="geology-inspector" class="geology-inspector" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
      </div>
      <p id="map-message" class="message" role="status"></p>

      <section class="profile-panel glass-regular" aria-labelledby="profile-heading">
        <div class="profile-heading">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">TRAVERSE ELEVATION TRANSECT</span><h2 id="profile-heading">Elevation Profile</h2></div>
          <span class="unit-label">DISTANCE · ELEVATION (METRES AREOID)</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="profile" role="img" aria-label="Elevation profile"></canvas>
        <p id="profile-summary" class="readout"></p>
        <p id="profile-inspection" class="profile-inspection" aria-live="polite">Hover the profile to inspect a distance and elevation sample.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="manual-analysis" class="manual-analysis glass-regular" aria-labelledby="manual-analysis-heading" hidden>
        <div class="profile-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">DRAWN POLYLINE · SAMPLED DEM</span><h2 id="manual-analysis-heading">Manual Route Terrain Analysis</h2></div></div>
        <p id="manual-analysis-status" class="manual-analysis-status" aria-live="polite">Draw and finish a route to analyze terrain.</p>
        <dl id="manual-analysis-metrics" class="manual-analysis-metrics"></dl>
        <ul id="manual-analysis-issues" class="warnings"></ul>
        <p id="manual-analysis-note" class="fine"></p>
        <h3 class="manual-profile-title">Manual route elevation profile</h3>
        <canvas id="manual-profile" role="img" aria-label="Manual route elevation profile"></canvas>
        <p id="manual-profile-inspection" class="profile-inspection" aria-live="polite">Hover the manual profile to inspect a terrain sample.</p>
      </section>
    </section>

    <section class="side-column glass-regular" aria-labelledby="routes-h">
      <span class="eyebrow">MISSION PLANNING</span><h2 id="routes-h">Plan a traverse</h2>
      <div class="points">
        <label>Start x (m) <input id="start-x" type="number" step="any"></label>
        <label>Start y (m) <input id="start-y" type="number" step="any"></label>
        <label>Destination x (m) <input id="goal-x" type="number" step="any"></label>
        <label>Destination y (m) <input id="goal-y" type="number" step="any"></label>
        <button id="apply-points" type="button">Apply points</button>
      </div>
      <p id="automatic-route-source" class="fine">Automatic routes use the selected MOLA or HiRISE elevation grid. CTX supports drawn-route sampling only. Routes are not astronaut-safety assessments.</p>
      <div id="route-list" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Route objectives"></div>
      <h3>Warnings for the selected route</h3>
      <ul id="warnings" class="warnings"></ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- Detailed Environmental, Scenario & Provenance Panels -->
  <section class="panels" aria-label="Details">
    <details id="panel-survival" open>
      <summary>Resource scenario arithmetic</summary>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <p class="note">This applies simple arithmetic to assumed consumable endurance. It is a planning demonstration, not a validated safety decision or astronaut-safety assessment.</p>
        <div class="grid3">
          <label>Suit power at start (%) <input id="res-power" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="90"> <output id="res-power-out">90</output></label>
          <label>Oxygen at start (%) <input id="res-o2" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="90"> <output id="res-o2-out">90</output></label>
          <label>Water at start (%) <input id="res-water" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="90"> <output id="res-water-out">90</output></label>
        </div>
        <div id="survival" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="panel-scenario">
      <summary>Scenario and assumptions</summary>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="grid3">
          <label>Local solar time (h) <input id="local-hour" type="range" min="0" max="24" step="0.25" value="12"> <output id="local-hour-out">12.00</output></label>
          <div><button id="use-now" type="button">Use the computed time at Jezero now</button></div>
          <label>Dust scenario <select id="dust"></select></label>
          <label>Radiation scenario <select id="radiation"></select></label>
          <label>Slope limit (°) <input id="max-slope" type="number" min="1" max="60" step="1" value="25"></label>
          <label>Flat walking speed (km/h) <input id="walk-speed" type="number" min="0.5" max="8" step="0.1" value="2.5"></label>
          <label>Required reserve after round trip (%) <input id="req-reserve" type="number" min="0" max="90" step="1" value="30"></label>
          <label>Power endurance at 100 % (h) <input id="end-power" type="number" min="1" max="48" step="0.5" value="8"></label>
          <label>Oxygen endurance at 100 % (h) <input id="end-o2" type="number" min="1" max="48" step="0.5" value="8"></label>
          <label>Water endurance at 100 % (h) <input id="end-water" type="number" min="1" max="48" step="0.5" value="10"></label>
        </div>
        <h3>Scenario values at the chosen time</h3>
        <table id="conditions"></table>
        <h3>Model parameters and where they come from</h3>
        <table id="params"></table>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="panel-science">
      <summary>Science targets</summary>
      <div class="panel-body" id="targets"></div>
    </details>

    <details id="panel-layers" open>
      <summary>Map layers</summary>
      <div class="panel-body layer-selector">
        <label class="layer-choice">Imagery
          <select id="imagery-layer" aria-describedby="imagery-layer-help">
            <option value="viking">Viking VIS global mosaic</option>
            <option value="off">Imagery off · shaded globe</option>
          </select>
          <span id="imagery-layer-help" class="fine">Global optical context, about 232 m/pixel. This is imagery, not elevation. Regional CTX and HiRISE optical mosaics are not rendered in the browser.</span>
        </label>
        <label class="layer-choice">Elevation and terrain analysis
          <select id="elevation-layer" aria-describedby="elevation-layer-help">
            <option value="mola">MOLA MEGDR · ~7.9 km planner cells</option>
            <option value="hirise">HiRISE DTM · ~20 m planner cells</option>
            <option value="ctx">CTX DEM · 20 m source posting · manual routes</option>
          </select>
          <span id="elevation-layer-help" class="fine">Slope is derived from the selected numerical elevation grid. MOLA and HiRISE support automatic routes; CTX supports manual drawn-route sampling only.</span>
        </label>
        <div id="elevation-status" class="layer-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <div class="ctx-status-row"><p id="ctx-terrain-status" class="layer-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p><button id="retry-ctx-analysis" type="button" hidden>Retry CTX</button></div>
        <p id="elevation-error" class="error" role="alert"></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="panel-data">
      <summary>Data &amp; Sources</summary>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div id="dataset-summary" class="dataset-summary" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <details id="technical-details">
          <summary>Technical details and provenance</summary>
          <div id="technical-summary" class="technical-summary"></div>
          <p class="fine">USGS Jezero geology is an interpreted regional map overlay, not a direct measurement. THEMIS (future qualitative thermal imagery), TES (optional coarse thermal inertia), CRISM (selected derived mineral products), and MEDA (archived observations for charts) are not integrated. Curiosity RAD is a Gale reference value; Mars24 is a time calculation. None of those is a Jezero map observation in this interface.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</main>
<footer class="site-footer"><p>Educational prototype made for the NASA Space Apps Challenge. It is not flight software and is not endorsed by NASA. Synthetic terrain is reserved for development tests; displayed scientific terrain products are labeled by source. See <code>DATA_SOURCES.md</code> and <code>AI_USAGE.md</code> in the repository.</p></footer>
